1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Across global geopolitics and maritime security,

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
no geographical choke point wields as much raw leverage

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,199
as the Strait of Hormuz.

4
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:11,700
Separating the rocky shores of Iran from the Arabian Peninsula,

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:15,599
this strategic passage narrows to barely 21 nautical miles

6
00:00:15,599 --> 00:00:17,400
at its critical gateway.

7
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,199
Every single day, over 21 million barrels of petroleum

8
00:00:21,199 --> 00:00:24,400
and liquefied natural gas traverse these waters,

9
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:29,199
accounting for more than 20 percent of total global petroleum consumption.

10
00:00:29,399 --> 00:00:34,200
Under international maritime law and the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea,

11
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,100
transit passage is technically guaranteed,

12
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:40,299
yet sovereign posturing and naval mind capabilities

13
00:00:40,299 --> 00:00:42,600
create an enduring flashpoint.

14
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,299
For the superpowers and global markets alike,

15
00:00:45,299 --> 00:00:47,600
any disruption in these contested waters

16
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,299
would immediately trigger catastrophic global energy inflation

17
00:00:51,299 --> 00:00:53,299
and economic paralysis.

